<section id="what">
  <h2>What a workspace is</h2>
  <p>Signing in for the first time creates a workspace called <strong>My Workspace</strong>, with you as its owner. Everything you connect belongs to it: repositories, pull requests, deployments and every metric derived from them.</p>
  <p>A workspace is <strong>not</strong> the same as a GitHub organisation. One workspace can track repositories from several organisations and personal accounts at once, and two people can track the same repository in their own separate workspaces without either seeing the other's.</p>
  <p>Rename a workspace at any time from <strong>Settings → Team</strong>.</p>
</section>

<section id="when-more">
  <h2>When you need more than one</h2>
  <p>Reach for a second workspace when the <em>audience</em> differs, not when the repositories do. A workspace is a boundary for people as much as for data.</p>
  <p>Here are some common scenarios where two workspaces are appropriate:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>An agency or consultancy</strong> keeping each client's delivery data separate.</li>
    <li><strong>Two organisations</strong> whose engineering leaders shouldn't see each other's numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>A personal sandbox</strong> alongside the company workspace you were invited to.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="managing">
  <h2>Creating and switching</h2>
  <p>Both live in the profile menu, top right.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create workspace makes a new, empty one with you as its owner, ready for its own GitHub connections.</li>
    <li>Switching reloads the dashboard with that workspace's data. Your choice is remembered for next time, and two browser tabs can sit in two different workspaces at once.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="leaving">
  <h2>Leaving and deleting</h2>
  <p>Here are the details for leaving and/or deleting workspaces:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Members can leave a workspace at any time from Settings → Team.</li>
    <li>Owners can transfer ownership to another member first and then leave as a member.</li>
    <li>A sole owner, meaning an owner with no other members, can delete the workspace from Settings → Team. It removes the workspace and all of its data permanently.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

